# Dockerfile.dockerignore beside this file cuts the context down to what the
# image reads: every workspace package the runner imports, whole, the
# manifest of every other one, the checkouts of superscalar and the HTTP
# runtime the workspace's root overrides their packages with, and the
# superscalar crates. BuildKit, Docker's default builder, reads it.
#
# The generated packages validate scalars through superscalar's Node addon,
# which no published package ships yet. The addon stage builds it for the
# image's platform from the superscalar checkout the naming file's [paths]
# scalar_typescript names, with the Rust release tools.env pins, against
# the glibc of the Debian release the Bun image runs on. The build stage puts
# it where superscalar's binding looks for it, builds the binding's and the
# HTTP runtime's dist/, which a checkout does not hold and which their
# packages export, and installs the workspace without its development
# packages: frozen to the lockfile, which fails when the lockfile does not
# match the packages the build wrote. A context without the lockfile, as in
# a project that has not committed it, resolves afresh and says so: two
# images of one commit may then differ. The generated CI's check refuses a
# missing or stale lockfile before any deploy. The image runs main.ts on the
# Bun release tools.env pins, as a non-root user.
#
# The runner opens the behavior engine (D58) through the engine's Node-API
# addon, which the image builds from source for its platform, with the
# crates the engine's Cargo workspace reaches by path at their places in
